---
import TextPage from '../../views/TextPage.astro';
import { company } from '../../data/company';
import { path } from '../../i18n/routes';
---

<TextPage
	route="privacy"
	heading="Personal data policy"
	lead="How we collect, use and protect your personal data, and how you can exercise your rights."
	updated={company.legalUpdated}
>
	<p>
		This policy covers the personal data {company.brand} processes through the jangol.com.co website and the Jangol for Gyms and Jangol
		for Schools platforms. It follows Colombian Statutory Law 1581 of 2012, Decree 1377 of 2013 (now part of Decree 1074 of 2015) and the
		other Colombian data protection rules. The Spanish version of this policy is the one that governs.
	</p>

	<h2>1. Data controller</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Company name: {company.legalName}</li>
		<li>Tax ID (NIT): {company.nit}</li>
		<li>Address: {company.address}, {company.city}, {company.country}</li>
		<li>Email for personal data matters: <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a></li>
		<li>Phone: {company.phone}</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>2. What data we collect</h2>
	<p>
		When you use the contact form we collect your name, your email, your company or school name if you give it, the product you are
		interested in and your message. The form does not ask for sensitive data, and we ask you not to include any in your message.
	</p>
	<p>
		When you visit the site, our network provider (Cloudflare) logs technical data such as your IP address, browser and the pages you
		visit, for security and aggregate measurement. The site does not use advertising cookies.
	</p>

	<h2>3. What we use your data for</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>To answer your request, set up a demo and send you the proposal you asked for.</li>
		<li>To follow up on that same request.</li>
		<li>To provide the service to clients who use our platforms or hire a custom project.</li>
		<li>To meet legal, accounting and tax obligations, such as electronic invoicing.</li>
		<li>To protect the site and the platforms from misuse.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>We do not sell your data, and we do not use it for other purposes without asking for a new authorization.</p>

	<h2>4. Data we process on behalf of our clients</h2>
	<p>
		Gyms and schools that use Jangol for Gyms or Jangol for Schools are the controllers of their members', students' and families' data.
		In that case {company.brand} acts as a processor: it handles that data only to provide the service, following the client's
		instructions and the contract signed with them. If you are a gym member or a school family and want to exercise your rights, you can
		contact the institution or write to us and we will pass your request on.
	</p>

	<h2>5. Data about children and teenagers</h2>
	<p>
		Jangol for Schools stores information about students under 18. That data is handled in the best interest of the minors and with
		respect for their fundamental rights, as Article 7 of Law 1581 of 2012 requires. The school obtains authorization from parents or legal
		guardians, and access is limited to the people who need the information for their role.
	</p>

	<h2>6. Your rights</h2>
	<p>Under Article 8 of Law 1581 of 2012 you can:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Know, update and correct your personal data.</li>
		<li>Ask for proof of the authorization you gave us.</li>
		<li>Be told how we have used your data.</li>
		<li>File complaints with the Superintendence of Industry and Commerce (SIC) for violations of the law.</li>
		<li>Revoke your authorization or ask us to delete your data, unless a legal or contractual duty requires us to keep it.</li>
		<li>Access your personal data free of charge.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>7. How to make a request or a complaint</h2>
	<p>
		Write to <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a> with your name, your ID number, a description of what you are asking
		for and a way to reach you.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>We answer requests within ten business days. If we need more time, we tell you why and answer within the next five business days.</li>
		<li>We resolve complaints within fifteen business days. If we need more time, we tell you why and answer within the next eight business days.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>If a complaint is incomplete, we ask you for what is missing within five business days of receiving it.</p>

	<h2>8. Providers and transfers</h2>
	<p>
		To run the site and the platforms we use infrastructure, email and form providers, some with servers outside Colombia. They include
		Cloudflare (site network and security) and Web3Forms (delivering the contact form to our inbox). We share only what each one needs to
		provide its service and require them to protect the information with measures equivalent to ours.
	</p>

	<h2>9. Security and retention</h2>
	<p>
		We protect information with encryption in transit, role-based access control and backups. We keep contact data while the business
		relationship or the request lasts, and afterwards only as long as accounting and tax rules require.
	</p>

	<h2>10. Authorization and changes to this policy</h2>
	<p>
		By ticking the authorization box on the <a href={path('contact', 'en')}>contact form</a> you agree to the processing of your data
		under this policy. If we change it in a significant way, we will publish the change on this page with a new update date.
	</p>
</TextPage>
